{
  "notes": "Cinematic, A mixolydian, 94 BPM. Sunrise over a machine city: a Berlin-school sequencer (a low resonant phase-distortion pluck rolling sixteenths on an A pedal: A, E and B, the open sus2 of the key), a synthetic choir that swells in on long attacks and breathes its vowel on a slow LFO, the player's bright sync lead on the Smart Keys (glide and a delayed vibrato), and a LinnDrum kit that arrives late: half-time with a big snare on 3, then straight and driving in the lift. Every chord is diatonic to the mixolydian and the major pentatonic is consonant over all of them. Scenes: A open sus2 voicings on I and VII; B the loop I v7 VII IV (the IV falls home to I); C the roots climb vi VII I to IV, the sequencer follows them and the choir's top voice rises; D strips to the choir on ii and IV. ENERGY opens the sequencer's filter and fills its sixteenths in, then brings the drums. All material is original.",
